-- title:
--   Base-changed X₁ function fields: compositum and equal relative degrees
-- statement:
--   Fix a field $L$ of characteristic zero and natural numbers $M,\ell,p$ with $M\neq 0$, $p\neq 0$, $3\le M$, $\ell$ prime and $\ell\nmid Mp$. For a level $N$, [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField N`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) is the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(N)$, namely the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 N)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and for an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))/\mathbb{Q}$, [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) is the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q))\to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$. The assertion is twofold. First, inside the lattice of intermediate fields of $L((q))/L$, the join of the base changes of the function fields of levels $Mp$ and $M\ell$ is the base change of the function field of level $M\ell p$. Second, the relative finrank of the base change of level $Mp$ inside the base change of level $M\ell p$ equals the relative finrank of the base change of level $M$ inside the base change of level $M\ell$; no numerical value for this common degree is asserted here, although the corresponding degree over $\mathbb{Q}$ is $\ell^2-1$.
--
--   Together the two clauses express the linear disjointness over the level-$M$ field of the level-$Mp$ and level-$M\ell$ $q$-expansion fields, with compositum the level-$M\ell p$ field, after base change of coefficients to $L$; the hypothesis $3\le M$ is needed, since for $M\le 2$ one has $-1\in\Gamma_1(M)$ and the degree equality fails. It is used in the construction of the pushout square describing the local structure of $X_1(Mp)$ along the level-raising map.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_laurentBaseChange_x1FunctionField_sup_levelRaise_eq_and_relfinrank_eq.lean

